The next closest hospital that you can go to that isn't Huntsville Hospital owned is

1347
01:42:50,240 --> 01:42:52,720
55 miles away in Coleman.

1348
01:42:52,720 --> 01:42:55,400
Who's going to Coleman?

1349
01:42:55,400 --> 01:42:57,400
Respectfully.

1350
01:42:57,400 --> 01:42:59,360
Okay.

1351
01:42:59,360 --> 01:43:04,760
Huntsville Hospital is blatantly in violation of several antitrust laws.

1352
01:43:04,760 --> 01:43:06,000
Let me be quite clear.

1353
01:43:06,000 --> 01:43:08,240
This is a crime.

1354
01:43:08,240 --> 01:43:10,320
It is against the FEC.

1355
01:43:10,320 --> 01:43:12,280
It is against the Clayton Act.

1356
01:43:12,280 --> 01:43:16,680
And to summarize, the Clayton Act, an illegal merger occurs when two companies join together

1357
01:43:16,680 --> 01:43:22,480
in a way that substantially lessen competition or tend to create a monopoly in a relevant

1358
01:43:22,480 --> 01:43:23,480
market.

1359
01:43:23,480 --> 01:43:28,120
This reduction in competition can harm consumers by potentially leading to higher prices or

1360
01:43:28,120 --> 01:43:30,320
fewer choices for products or services.

1361
01:43:30,320 --> 01:43:34,640
It can also harm workers by potentially leading to lower wages or fewer choices for employment.

1362
01:43:34,640 --> 01:43:40,680
And this is just one example of the laws broken by Huntsville Hospital and their very large

1363
01:43:40,680 --> 01:43:41,680
system.

1364
01:43:41,680 --> 01:43:46,440
The monopoly increases risk for patients and staff alike, with staff too afraid to speak

1365
01:43:46,440 --> 01:43:51,240
up when management demands unsafe ratios and when staff can't take off medically recommended

1366
01:43:51,240 --> 01:43:56,080
time to recover from their own health issues due to restrictive time off policies, it is

1367
01:43:56,080 --> 01:43:58,800
an increase of accidents in patient care.

1368
01:43:58,800 --> 01:44:03,960
How can we expect them to be able to take care of us if they can't take care of themselves?

1369
01:44:03,960 --> 01:44:10,200
The maternity floor cannot take the recommended time off at Huntsville Hospital because they

1370
01:44:10,200 --> 01:44:15,880
have no paid parental leave, maternity or paternity at all.

1371
01:44:15,880 --> 01:44:18,400
It's all unpaid.

1372
01:44:18,400 --> 01:44:24,120
We cannot reasonably expect people to be able to take the time off in this economy without

1373
01:44:24,120 --> 01:44:26,000
paid leave.

1374
01:44:26,000 --> 01:44:32,960
And that's one of the several ways they underpay their employees, on top of the fact that new

1375
01:44:32,960 --> 01:44:41,320
nurses make more money than nurses that they are studying after.

1376
01:44:41,320 --> 01:44:46,720
When the pay bump goes up, the nurses that actually work there currently do not receive

1377
01:44:46,720 --> 01:44:51,000
that pay bump in their base pay.

1378
01:44:51,000 --> 01:44:52,080
That's not how that works.

1379
01:44:52,080 --> 01:44:56,360
So the new nurses who come in get paid more than the old nurses, so then the old nurses

1380
01:44:56,360 --> 01:45:01,560
quit, leave the entire region of this state, and then all we have is new nurses.

1381
01:45:01,560 --> 01:45:06,960
Hey, I'd rather have a nurse who's been in the same place for 15 years working than a

1382
01:45:06,960 --> 01:45:11,200
nurse that's been working for two years, who is just here to collect years of experience

1383
01:45:11,200 --> 01:45:12,640
so that they can leave too.

1384
01:45:12,640 --> 01:45:14,480
Thank you for your comments.

1385
01:45:14,480 --> 01:45:15,480
