1723
02:05:53,320 --> 02:06:03,720
Mr. Hamilton, share with us what we're accomplishing here.

1724
02:06:03,720 --> 02:06:07,000
Good evening Council Members, John Hamilton, City Administrator.

1725
02:06:07,000 --> 02:06:11,080
So what's before you is an item that I would describe it as corrective.

1726
02:06:11,080 --> 02:06:15,240
It's something that we should have brought to you some time ago related to the entry

1727
02:06:15,240 --> 02:06:24,280
level step, so on the pay scale, for our police and fire candidates that come in as lateral

1728
02:06:24,280 --> 02:06:25,280
transfers.

1729
02:06:25,280 --> 02:06:31,280
And so what we mean by lateral is we have a fair number of both officers, police officers

1730
02:06:31,280 --> 02:06:38,160
and firefighters who had served in other cities, other either law enforcement or fire service

1731
02:06:38,160 --> 02:06:43,440
positions elsewhere and had some number of years of experience, wanted to transfer into

1732
02:06:43,440 --> 02:06:48,800
Huntsville and so we hired them in relying on that prior training and that prior experience.

1733
02:06:48,800 --> 02:06:52,340
We're bringing in more experienced personnel through this system.

1734
02:06:52,340 --> 02:07:01,600
So a few years ago we brought you an action to set by ordinance the minimum entry step

1735
02:07:01,600 --> 02:07:04,480
for brand new candidates.

1736
02:07:04,480 --> 02:07:07,680
And so that first section you see there on that spreadsheet where it says COH from the

1737
02:07:07,680 --> 02:07:08,720
beginning.

1738
02:07:08,720 --> 02:07:14,440
So that is what the ordinance currently does for a candidate who has never served previously

1739
02:07:14,440 --> 02:07:18,280
in law enforcement or fire brand new rookie coming into our school.

1740
02:07:18,280 --> 02:07:22,660
So what happens right now, for both those departments they go through a rigorous hiring

1741
02:07:22,660 --> 02:07:23,960
process.

1742
02:07:23,960 --> 02:07:29,240
When they start the academy they come in at step eight within the appropriate grade.

1743
02:07:29,240 --> 02:07:34,760
And once they've completed all their training, the academy as well as other in-service training

1744
02:07:34,760 --> 02:07:41,600
required and they're ready to actually go into full service for our city, they're promoted

1745
02:07:41,600 --> 02:07:43,460
to a step 12.

1746
02:07:43,460 --> 02:07:46,620
And then like every employee in the city when they hit their one year anniversary they get

1747
02:07:46,620 --> 02:07:49,000
a step increase second year anniversary on down.

1748
02:07:49,000 --> 02:07:56,360
So that first row is that the ordinance currently reads for police coming in or for police or

1749
02:07:56,360 --> 02:07:59,680
firefighters coming in in that circumstance.

1750
02:07:59,680 --> 02:08:04,500
What's below that is the current situation for someone who's coming in as a lateral.

1751
02:08:04,500 --> 02:08:10,060
So we could have somebody who's in another city, Alabama or otherwise, we have folks

1752
02:08:10,060 --> 02:08:15,320
come in from other states but most of our lawyers come from other parts of the state

1753
02:08:15,320 --> 02:08:20,400
and they could have up to five years of experience and right now they come in as a step nine.

1754
02:08:20,400 --> 02:08:25,580
And that's the way it was prior to the amendment that y'all did a few years ago that set that

1755
02:08:25,580 --> 02:08:26,580
top rate.

1756
02:08:26,580 --> 02:08:31,420
So when I say it's corrective, we should have at the time that we had you change the

1757
02:08:31,420 --> 02:08:36,880
ordinance for brand new candidates, we should have also made a similar change to those coming

1758
02:08:36,880 --> 02:08:38,500
in as laterals and we failed to do something.

1759
02:08:38,500 --> 02:08:42,880
So this is us coming in trying to fix what we should have already done, quite frankly,

1760
02:08:42,880 --> 02:08:44,800
just to be completely transparent with you.

1761
02:08:44,800 --> 02:08:49,980
But right now today, as you see a brand new officer who's gone through our academy has

1762
02:08:49,980 --> 02:08:54,680
now going his very first day ever serving in law enforcement as a step 12, but someone

1763
02:08:54,680 --> 02:09:00,520
who might have served in some other city with five years is coming in as a step nine.

1764
02:09:00,520 --> 02:09:05,600
Clearly step nine is not within our system appropriately acknowledging their service.

1765
02:09:05,600 --> 02:09:09,200
And we're only bringing in someone who has served well, who's highly qualified that we

1766
02:09:09,200 --> 02:09:11,300
very much want to add to our department.

1767
02:09:11,300 --> 02:09:22,480
And so we are failing to acknowledge that service in our current structure.

1768
02:09:22,480 --> 02:09:28,000
So that's what you see there on the 12, step 12 for brand new as compared to nine, 10 or

1769
02:09:28,000 --> 02:09:31,080
11, depending on their years of service in our current system.

1770
02:09:31,080 --> 02:09:36,400
And so if you look, you know, five years in, one of somebody who's had all five years of

1771
02:09:36,400 --> 02:09:41,280
service with us is now a step 17, someone who had five years of service previously,

1772
02:09:41,280 --> 02:09:43,200
now five years less is still only a step 14.

1773
02:09:43,200 --> 02:09:49,080
So you see that within our current process, we are failing to acknowledge that prior service

1774
02:09:49,080 --> 02:09:52,780
and that experience they brought to our team.

1775
02:09:52,780 --> 02:09:57,640
So go into what is proposed, what's before you right now, that top line stays the same.

1776
02:09:57,640 --> 02:10:02,400
That is the ordinance as it currently reads for someone who's coming in brand new into

1777
02:10:02,400 --> 02:10:08,760
that service and what's before you, it sets a new salary, entry level salary structure

1778
02:10:08,760 --> 02:10:10,160
for those that might lateral in.

1779
02:10:10,160 --> 02:10:14,160
And you see, we actually break it out by year of service.

1780
02:10:14,160 --> 02:10:15,760
So they have to have completed those years.

1781
02:10:15,760 --> 02:10:19,480
So for example, somebody has two and a half years, we're going to give them only credit

1782
02:10:19,480 --> 02:10:20,680
for four years of service.

1783
02:10:20,680 --> 02:10:25,600
So they would come in as two years of service, three, four, five on down through eight.

1784
02:10:25,600 --> 02:10:30,640
And what we set out to do here is one, appropriately acknowledge that service that they previously

1785
02:10:30,640 --> 02:10:33,960
provided and the experience they're bringing to the team, but also acknowledge that there

1786
02:10:33,960 --> 02:10:37,080
is value in someone who has served all those years in Huntsville.

1787
02:10:37,080 --> 02:10:42,760
So what this does, so someone who came in brand new to the service with the city of

1788
02:10:42,760 --> 02:10:46,320
Huntsville, three years then there'd be a step 15.

1789
02:10:46,320 --> 02:10:50,920
Someone who is laterally in with three years of service would be one step behind that.

1790
02:10:50,920 --> 02:10:53,400
So we could, I'm giving you one example there.

1791
02:10:53,400 --> 02:10:56,360
We could do this for every single one of those examples.

1792
02:10:56,360 --> 02:11:01,360
A brand new person coming in with prior service would be one step behind where they would

1793
02:11:01,360 --> 02:11:03,840
have been if they'd had all those years with Huntsville.

1794
02:11:03,840 --> 02:11:07,360
Acknowledge, and there is a learning curve associated with just learning the community

1795
02:11:07,360 --> 02:11:10,760
and things, but we also want to acknowledge that prior service.

1796
02:11:10,760 --> 02:11:15,040
Now there's really two layers to this that we've got before you.

1797
02:11:15,040 --> 02:11:20,620
One is within our system, within our structure, we believe and we recommend that this better

1798
02:11:20,620 --> 02:11:24,920
acknowledges that prior service and that experience they bring to the team and better

1799
02:11:24,920 --> 02:11:31,280
aligns their compensation with their fellow police and firefighters that are in our service.

1800
02:11:31,280 --> 02:11:33,480
The other thing that it also does is makes us more competitive.

1801
02:11:33,480 --> 02:11:38,520
What we have found, and I think y'all are well aware of the challenges of recruiting

1802
02:11:38,520 --> 02:11:42,600
folks into public safety across our country right now, but we've experienced that issue

1803
02:11:42,600 --> 02:11:44,160
here.

1804
02:11:44,160 --> 02:11:48,740
This is an example where we have fallen behind in our compensation package with our surrounding

1805
02:11:48,740 --> 02:11:49,880
communities.

1806
02:11:49,880 --> 02:11:55,040
And so what this does is much better aligns us with all the other departments that we

1807
02:11:55,040 --> 02:11:59,720
partner with that surround us, but they're our partners, but they're also our competitors

1808
02:11:59,720 --> 02:12:02,480
in terms of hiring highly qualified people.

1809
02:12:02,480 --> 02:12:08,280
And so this will also align us much better in terms of being able to recruit highly qualified

1810
02:12:08,280 --> 02:12:11,520
folks, both police and firefighters into our service.

1811
